# Copy this file to `.env.llm` and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.llm.example .env.llm
#
# `.env.llm` is gitignored (this template is not) and is picked up
# automatically by `capmap agent` — it walks up from the instance directory
# to find the closest `.env.llm`, so one shared file at the repo root or a
# per-instance override both work. A real shell `export` always takes
# priority over anything in the file.
#
# You only need to fill in the section for the backend you are using — see
# README.md's "对话式操作：capmap agent" section for the full picture.

# --- openai backend (default — OpenAI itself, or any gateway that speaks
# --- the same /chat/completions format: Portkey, LiteLLM, Azure OpenAI) ---
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=<your-api-key>
# OPENAI_MODEL=<model-id-exactly-as-your-endpoint-expects-it>   # no default — deployment-specific
# OPENAI_EXTRA_HEADER=x-portkey-api-key
#   ^ only needed if your gateway wants the key on a non-standard header too
#     (Portkey does — set it to x-portkey-api-key). Most OpenAI-compatible
#     endpoints authenticate fine with the standard Bearer header alone and
#     do not need this set at all.

# --- anthropic backend (calls the Claude API directly, needs --backend anthropic
# --- or CAPMAP_AGENT_BACKEND=anthropic below since openai is now the default) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CAPMAP_AGENT_MODEL=claude-opus-5              # optional — this is already the default

# --- optional: force a backend instead of relying on the openai default ---
# CAPMAP_AGENT_BACKEND=anthropic                # or: openai
